CODEGENGAPS - expressions the compiler cannot build, with repro source

Every case below was verified against the installed compiler on
2026-08-15, compiled as:

	/usr/local/bin/ccc -m micronix -O -c repro.c

All of them came out of porting the 2.11BSD userland (cat tee cmp ln
chmod chgrp du date dd mv pr od grep sed ...) - real code the PDP-11
compiler swallowed and this one does not.  Each entry gives the
smallest source that still fails, the exact diagnostic, and the
workaround the port used, so the ported sources can be unwound when
the rule is added.

Three kinds, and the distinction is the point of the layout: WRONG
CODE entries compile silently and compute the wrong thing - those
are the ones that cost afternoons; "no rule" entries fail loudly on
legitimate expressions; and the last section is refusals the
compiler is entitled to, recorded only so the diagnostic is
recognized on sight.

FIXED entries keep their repro and their diagnosis: the repro is the
regression test, and the diagnosis is why the next one like it will
be found faster.  The workarounds noted in each can be unwound in the
ported sources.

