Fails:

	char buffer[9000];
	char *colp[72];
	f(i)
	int i;
	{
		register char **p;

		p = &colp[i];
		if (*p >= buffer)
			*p = buffer;
		return 0;
	}

Also fails with the comparison spelled `*p == &buffer[9000]`.

Compiles, for calibration - each is the same function with one thing
